schema conversion:
use SCT to do it first, then manually review 2333...
SQL Server	        PostgreSQL	                        Usually auto-converted?	        Notes
INT IDENTITY	        GENERATED ... AS IDENTITY / SERIAL	✅	                        PostgreSQL Identity is recommended for new projects rather than SERIAL.
BIT	                BOOLEAN	                                ✅	                        Usually straightforward.
NVARCHAR(MAX)	        TEXT	                                ✅	                        Usually straightforward.
DATETIME	        TIMESTAMP	                        ✅	                        Verify the intended time-zone semantics.
UNIQUEIDENTIFIER	UUID	                                ✅	                        Usually straightforward.
[ColumnName]	        columnname / "ColumnName"	        ✅	                        Pay close attention to case sensitivity.
dbo	                public	                                ✅ / ⚠️	                        Don't automatically change dbo to public; the target schema should be decided based on the application's design.
GO	                ;	                                ✅ / ⚠️	                        GO is not SQL. It is a batch separator used by SQL Server client tools. It cannot always be replaced directly with ;.
GETDATE()	        CURRENT_TIMESTAMP / NOW()	        ✅	                        Usually straightforward.
ISNULL()	        COALESCE()	                        ✅	                        Usually straightforward, but type behavior and semantics should be verified.
@@ROWCOUNT	        GET DIAGNOSTICS ... ROW_COUNT	        ⚠️	                        Cannot be replaced one-to-one. The surrounding logic usually needs to be rewritten.

